WEBVTT

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.660
There!

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.740
With this. Now we're the same!

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.170
Yeah.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:04.860
The dangerous forest invites me
It's showtime again tonight

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.730
(Ayakashi NIGHT)

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:11.930
Everyone's rampaging
with all their strength

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.830
(Fighting late into the night)

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.270
Drive away all hesitation

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.680
Wanna take them on? Yeah

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.210
I will protect you
(No matter what)

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.550
I will protect you, that's all
(that's all I want)

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:34.220
Goodbye to the days
when all I'd do was cry

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.720
Sha la la la la...

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:45.130
I hold words in my heart
that I'd like to say

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:47.100
(Secret romance)

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:52.310
Standing in front of me is someone
I don't want to lose

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.070
(A strange distance)

00:01:54.540 --> 00:02:00.910
I can't stand watching
people get hurt anymore

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:01.980
Yeah

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.450
I wanna be your knight
(I wanna be strong)

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:09.060
I wanna be your light
(More than I am now)

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.390
Someday I'll share with you
my 100% smile

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:33.770
Hey!

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.120
Don't "hey" me.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.680
Besides, why are we meeting here
of all places?

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.180
I wanted an ice cream float.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.050
You of all people... With that face?
An ice cream float?

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.560
I can't drink something
with my face...

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:48.850
I have to use my mouth.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.730
What I'm saying is that you
stick out like a sore thumb here.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:53.860
I'll have a kelp tea.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:56.070
You don't dress that
differently from me.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.100
What are you saying?
I'm fine.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.730
I'm sorry.
We only have black tea.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.940
What? Oh fine.
Then I'll have that.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:06.100
Would you like lemon tea
or milk tea?

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.570
I don't care.
Either one is fine!

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.150
Are you mad?

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.450
It's because I don't
want to see you.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.460
Let's get this over with.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.190
There's no mistake that
your organization's Number Three

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.220
leaked the information about you
joining the Executive Committee.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:27.340
The one pulling the strings
is mentioned in here.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.600
To the best of my knowledge.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.900
Correct.
You did a great job investigating.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:36.740
"Correct"?

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.480
But it's inaccurate to call it
"your organization."

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.150
You're a member of
the Night Troops now.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.850
So who do you think
is pulling the strings?

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.790
Possibly... someone on
the Executive Committee.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.830
So have you found any information
on the committee members?

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.000
I've only heard rumors.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.500
Their information is
considered top secret.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:05.700
Only a handful of people
know who they are.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:06.830
Do something about it.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.500
Hey! Do you know how dangerous
it is to pry into their affairs?

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:12.940
You can handle it.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.720
Isn't one of your relatives
on the Executive Committee?

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.920
There's going to be
a committee meeting soon.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:24.990
Yomi. Yomi.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.360
Can you find out about it
before then?

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:32.020
You can do it, right?

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.560
By the way, I am very nice.
To my friends, that is.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.430
You two are completely different.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.510
Are you really Yoshimori's brother?

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:50.140
We are. By birth.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.880
All right, let's start class!

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.940
Stand.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.520
Hey, Sumimura. Class is starting.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.460
At least stand up.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:04.690
Bow.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.540
What is that?

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.090
Be seated.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.400
We're going to start
a new section today.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.010
No wonder no one noticed.
It's a ghost.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.880
Is it possessing the teacher?

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.240
What's wrong, Sumimura?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.040
Have you ever had a cat?

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:31.890
Ask me questions related to class.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.220
By the way,
I've only had a Marimo.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.960
Marimo?
Is that the name of the cat?

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.470
That cat is so cute.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.570
Okay, Kanda, read the next section.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.710
Y-Yes.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.910
In autumn, the evening...

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:57.410
the blazing sun has sunk very close
to the mountain rim. And uh...

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.610
He's possessed all right.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.820
I better get it away
from the school soon,

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.950
but it's a lot of work separating
ghosts and humans.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:09.450
And helping its spirit pass on
is even more work.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:11.590
All right...
What should I do?

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:15.300
All right...
What should we do?

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.010
We have a newcomer today, right?

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:21.210
The seats will be filled
for the first time in ages.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.730
I hear he is very young.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.240
I cannot wait.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:30.390
But does he have the capability,
befitting of the seat?

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.820
Watch your mouth!
He was the President's choice.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:34.960
It doesn't matter.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.630
If we don't like him, we can just...

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.360
He might die before
he even reaches here.

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.460
Oh? You're playing tricks again?

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.930
Cheap pranks.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:00.580
He saw right through it.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.910
Darned youngster.

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:04.450
You have failed horribly.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:24.290
I am honored to join
the Council of Twelve.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.530
My name is Masamori Sumimura.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.910
I may be inexperienced,
but I will continue

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:30.910
to improve myself
so that I may fulfill

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.500
- the responsibilities of this seat.
- He's young.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.780
- I hope you will give me further guidance
- He is Chief of the Night Troops?

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.650
- And encouragement in the future.
- Those barbaric half-wits?

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:40.650
Barbaric? They are more like
a collection of naïve children.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:43.830
The Night Troops are nothing
but a collection of outcasts

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.520
within the Shadow Organization.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.400
The President is absent today.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:53.930
It is rare for him to attend meetings
in the first place.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.590
We can hold off on
the introductions for now.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.810
Your seat is over there.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:00.400
Yes.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.120
Would you please look under
your seat cushion?

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.260
That is yours.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.360
It's a membership badge of sorts.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.170
Please hold onto it.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.460
It just so happens that
the seventh seat was vacant.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.340
The number itself holds
no special meaning.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:39.670
You will be Number Seven
in this council.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.480
Numbers may not hold meaning,

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:47.150
but do not think that you have the same
speaking rights as the rest of us.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.260
By the way, if you lose or damage it,
you will be demoted.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.130
Please be careful.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:10.100
This place is a den of monsters.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.100
It'll become a monster?

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:15.580
Yeah.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.680
When animal ghosts stay in Karasumori,
they'll eventually become Ayakashi.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.320
Then what are you going to do?

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.550
That's too cruel.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:28.260
Yeah. I don't want to do it either.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:30.460
But separating the ghost
might be really hard.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:31.860
But it's possible, right?

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:36.730
Yeah. There must be a reason
why that cat is so fixated on him.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.070
I have to ask what that reason is.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:40.760
Like with "meows"?

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:45.770
No! I have to ask the teacher.
Cats don't talk.

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.550
So if you don't do that,
it'll turn into a monster cat?

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:53.280
But it's so cute.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.280
Mr. Kurosu!

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.920
What is it?
You seemed awake today.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:05.060
Um, I have a question.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.360
What?
You have a question for me?

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:10.630
You can ask me as much
as you want.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:14.140
I was thinking of getting a cat.

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:14.810
Huh?

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:18.070
So what's it like to have a cat?

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.880
I thought you had
a question relating to class,

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.440
since you were awake for once...

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.540
I'm serious!
Please answer me!

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.980
I told you.
I've only kept a Marimo as a pet.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.290
Why are you asking me this?

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.760
There are other people
you can ask.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:36.620
What are you saying?
You're the only one I can ask.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.860
I thought teachers were
the adults closest to kids.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:42.630
True. But it sounds insincere
when you say it.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.540
Come on.
Trust your students more.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.470
Then why don't you participate
in class more?

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:56.140
Come here!

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:59.080
What are you doing
all of a sudden?

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:00.310
That's a ghost.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:02.520
That doesn't make it all right
for you to eliminate it on sight!

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.520
All ghosts in Karasumori
should be eliminated.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:09.130
I want to eliminate that messed up
thought process of yours.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.120
Sumimura!

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:11.900
I don't really know
what you're up to,

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:15.130
but if you have questions,
come to the teacher's lounge after school.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:19.430
I don't understand.
Those things cause problems.

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:21.310
It's also possessing someone.

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:24.610
It'll affect him if you don't do
something about it.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.240
That's why...

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.060
Besides, it's because you...

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.220
Did you two do something again?

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:41.920
Listen to me. Tokine...

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:47.930
I think Gen is right.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.730
You have got to be kidding me!

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:54.040
He's right, but we're the ones
in charge of Karasumori.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.570
Th-That's right.
Let me take care of it.

00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:59.310
Stupid people have their own
stupid way of solving problems.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:01.140
Yeah! Stupid people have
their own stupid...

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.880
You're not helping.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:05.820
Then do it.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:08.080
If you can figure out how to
take care of it without eliminating it.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.820
All right! I'll show you!

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.420
About the Karasumori issue...

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.370
Fortunately, we have a member of
the Sumimura family with us.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:23.770
He should know much.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:26.540
Though he is not
the Legitimate Heir.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:35.540
I see...
So it's about cats again.

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:39.550
I keep telling you that
I've only had a pet Marimo before.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:41.480
Do you want to see it?

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.450
I-It's a Marimo algae ball, all right.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:45.350
And it even says "Lake Akan" on it.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.990
Go ask the other teachers.
There's nothing I can tell you.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:54.570
Actually, I'm interested in cats,
but not just any cat. It's about black cats!

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:56.260
Oh?

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.170
All right!
He's interested now!

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:00.430
Are you okay?

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:03.900
Th-That's why I wanted to talk about it.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:07.140
M-My family is against it because
they say that black cats are bad luck.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:08.920
You're right.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:11.180
Black cats are widely
considered to be bad luck.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.610
But depending on the region,
they can be a sign of good luck, too.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:16.550
Oh, really?

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.250
Nice. He's starting to talk.

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:20.380
Speaking of which...

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:23.960
There was a black cat that
used to come here.

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.060
It wasn't very friendly, though.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:30.040
I complimented it on its fur and such,
every time I saw it,

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.130
and eventually it grew fond of me.

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:36.610
What do you mean
by complimenting it?

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.270
It's one of the basics of wooing.
Remember that.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.070
Come to think of it.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.280
I haven't seen that cat recently.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.610
I wonder how it's doing.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:53.690
I've been too busy to
go outside and read lately.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:03.040
Cats always want compliments
from someone

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.800
despite how much they put on airs.

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.130
Stop putting on airs.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.840
You called me because
you found something.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.140
Hurry up and talk.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.650
What is that skin?

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:20.450
Calm down.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:23.890
Nothing good ever comes
from rushing things.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.160
No, thank you.
I'll add the sugar myself.

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:30.190
What is this?!

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.160
You're so funny.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:33.630
Don't poke fun at me!

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:36.270
I tried to restore it just
to see if I could.

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:38.500
What do you think?
It's quite adorable, no?

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:41.370
There's a tiny demon inside.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.100
This is very well made.

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:46.110
Can you feel any Negative Energy
emanating from it?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.270
No...

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:48.880
That's the point here.

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:53.210
This skin almost completely
shuts out the scent of Ayakashi.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:56.290
It also serves as a sort
of protective layer.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:15:00.830
It enables the Ayakashi to
move around during the day.

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.490
They can now move during the day?

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:07.090
But there are problems with it.
Try blowing fire.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:15.970
It has some some problems
with durability.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.710
There's a limit to how long
they can use it, too.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:23.340
Their powers are
greatly restricted as well.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.850
Try to blow fire once more.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:33.520
I suppose they are still
in the process of developing this.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:35.790
Developing? For what?

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:42.300
They probably made it initially to fool
people like you who can smell Ayakashi.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.900
To deceive you.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:48.440
But now I think their motives
are a bit different.

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:52.540
Different?
What are the Kokuboro plotting?

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:55.450
Oh? You know about the Kokuboro?

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:56.640
That's unexpected.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:57.880
Don't take me for a fool.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:00.250
I've been doing
my own research as well.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:03.780
I was planning on keeping you
in suspense to the very end.

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.420
Stop this and just talk!

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:11.030
I think this is all part of
a grand experiment.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:12.490
An experiment?

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:17.840
Did you know that the Kokuboro are
spreading rumors about Karasumori?

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:20.330
Yes. I know.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:25.340
There is one interesting piece
of information they use to lure others.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:29.240
After hearing this,
I thought, how times have changed.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.510
Hurry up and say it!

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:35.320
Well, they claim that the ones
who work hard for them

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:37.760
will be rewarded by being
turned into a human.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:41.660
We now live in times when
Ayakashi are striving to become human.

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:51.000
I've heard of people turning into Ayakashi,
but never the reverse.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.540
Times have certainly
become very entertaining.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.810
You're the only one
that's enjoying this.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:01.210
I know you want to become
an Ayakashi-geezer eventually.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.150
I can't.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:07.580
I've done too many things to make me
despised by both people and Ayakashi.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.320
We still have a mountain
of problems before us.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.330
It'll be fine.

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:15.300
But you should use the Shadow
Organization as much as you can.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.850
I'm sure they can help.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:21.200
I can't leave this matter to them!
They're hopeless.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:25.010
Come now. I know that
you're estranged from them,

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.560
but don't tell me
you didn't know.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:29.210
Masamori-kun is now the youngest
Executive Committee member

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.140
of the Shadow Organization.

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:33.040
Wh-What?

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:36.280
It seems that
the Shadow Organization

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.250
has no intention of leaving
Karasumori alone.

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:41.780
So many things are happening
in Karasumori.

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:44.150
Are you sure Yoshimori-kun
can handle it?

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:46.920
He'll be fine.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:51.130
He's different from Masamori.
But he has his good points.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:58.040
FACULTY LOUNGE
Goodbye. See you tomorrow.

00:17:58.970 --> 00:17:59.960
Aoki-Sensai.

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:01.060
Yes?

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:02.910
Um, do you remember
the black cat

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.640
that was often on the grass patch
behind the science lab?

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:07.480
Is it still there?

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:11.510
Oh. That cat died.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:17.120
The other day,
during a rainy afternoon

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.120
it was hit by a car
in front of the school.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.490
It's getting dark.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.970
Are you gonna wait until
that teacher goes home?

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.370
Shut up.

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:50.080
You certainly have
a beautiful black coat.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:53.290
Starting today,
your name is Noir.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:56.560
Did you know?
That means "black" in French.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.500
Look over here, Noir.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:04.130
The shape of your tail is perfect.
So elegant.

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:10.270
Goodness!
Even your sneeze is perfection!

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.040
Seems like the distance between us
is only five centimeters now!

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.890
Why don't you get on my lap?

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:24.190
Wait! Ow!
Why my shoulders?

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:35.190
That's...

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:43.040
Is this a parting gift from Noir?

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.340
You did well. Noir.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:14.870
It passed on...

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:19.350
That cat probably just wanted
one last compliment from him.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:28.220
It's good that it didn't transform,
so you didn't have to do anything, after all.

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:32.850
Yeah. I'm glad I didn't have to.

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:37.690
I wonder what the Chief
would've done.

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:43.870
Let's end the meeting here
for today.

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:50.840
None of them may be
human anymore.

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:55.710
Regarding Karasumori,
it has been appointed to you.

00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:57.950
But if you make any mistake,

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.320
the Senior Executives
will have to take action.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:02.950
Be sure that you do not
increase our work.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.310
I understand.

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:06.890
The Kokuboro can be a formidable foe.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:09.350
Can you really fight them
off yourself?

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:15.190
Oh. Come on.
Bullying the newcomer already?

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:16.530
Are you okay?

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:24.030
Just when I thought
I had your badge...

00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:27.110
Come now.
You should stop right there.

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:30.010
Sumimura-kun, I wish you luck.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:31.390
We have high hopes for you.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:35.910
As long as you know your place,
you may survive a bit longer.

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:39.450
Don't be deceived by his kind words.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:42.830
He's been here the longest.

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:48.460
Don't upset the harmony.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:50.530
Let's work together
and have fun!

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:05.510
So that was the Council of Twelve
that control the Shadow Organization?

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:11.250
They're laughable.

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:16.790
They have powers like monsters
yet they fear a little change?

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:20.790
They must have forgotten long ago what
it's like to be an ordinary human!

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:23.930
I will take care of everything
without fail.

00:22:24.270 --> 00:22:27.400
I won't let those Ayakashi get
anywhere near Karasumori.

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:32.070
Do they really think I would step aside
and do nothing about it?

00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:50.860
With a look on your face that says,
"I'm doing this for you"

00:22:50.900 --> 00:22:54.130
While being enthusiastic
across the table

00:22:54.270 --> 00:22:58.290
Why do you only tell me
dark predictions?

00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:01.900
It's a meaningless
use of language.

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:05.700
Trying to avoid an emergency,
nothing's gonna happen

00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:09.680
I can't learn anything
(What's going on?)

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:13.740
You're not bearing
the brunt of my future

00:23:13.790 --> 00:23:17.020
I am, it's common sense

00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:21.360
I can't go anywhere
if I'm always weak

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:27.330
Train me so hard until I cry

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:33.670
If you're gonna complain that
tough times are heading our way

00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:35.640
(if that's true)

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:40.340
Please don't baby me
any more than you need to

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:43.780
Please Please Please

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:47.980
Even if I bleed
I'll get a hold of the wisdom

00:23:48.020 --> 00:23:51.320
To stand firm in
this unstable world

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:55.590
You watch from far away

00:23:55.630 --> 00:24:01.590
It's strange that
I want to hold you

00:24:02.400 --> 00:24:03.700
Hey Hey
